 ```
 
+### Compound Format
+
+Set `compound` to combine multiple units, largest first. Days are the largest unit and seconds the smallest, so leftover milliseconds are dropped and anything under one second becomes `"0s"`. Zero-valued parts are skipped. It only applies to the short format; `long: true` takes precedence.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })               // "1h 30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })              // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(3601000, { compound: true })               // "1h 1s"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })              // "-1h 30m"
+ms(1999, { compound: true })                  // "1s"
+ms(500, { compound: true })                   // "0s"
+ms(5400000, { compound: true, long: true })   // "2 hours"
+```
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
